year":2024,"record_id":"MLDB-000663","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity (logP) of the ruthenium(II) compounds was determined using the shake – flask method [42]. At first, aqueous (0.9 % w/v) sodium chloride and organic (n–octanol) phases were saturated for 1 week. The tested ruthenium(II) compounds were dissolved in the organic phase, keeping the concentration at the level of 0.03 mg/mL. The organic phase was analysed using UV – Vis spectroscopy before and after shaking with 0.9 % NaClaq to determine the concentration of the compound. The absorption values before and after shaking were compared, and, based on the Lambert–Beer Law, the partition coefficient for each compound was calculated to determine the logP values. The procedures were repeated fivefold. The error bars presented in the chart are based on the calculated standard deviations."}]}